            "review_title": "Review at Banh My Pho Hue",
            "review_text": "pojke-fredde\nBrussels, Belgium574 contributions\n0\nTasty and cheap typical bánh mi\nMay 2024 • Solo\nSo, I am not sure I fully get the banh mi obsession here. Reviewers on TA and elsewhere are raving about crunchy baguettes (the smaller version we back home call piccolo’s for some reason) with fluffy white bread inside. That’s, frankly how all baguettes should be and they typically are where in Europe they’re sold. \n\nWhat’s different is the non-descript liver pâté and an adventurous jet of Chili sauce. \nSo yes this banh mi was really tasty and mostly locals often queue as you can see on the pics here, and at 30k VND they are really cheap but that won’t make this quick ‘n simple lunch a national heritage culinary delight, if you ask me.\n\nNonetheless, if you’d like to sample a good one with local flavours and couleur locale, you can’t go wrong here.\nRead more\nWritten May 18, 2024",
            "rating": 4.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
