            "review_text": "George P\nNew York City, New York14 contributions\n1\nSimple, delicious, super fast and very good!\nDec 2014 • Friends\nI can't believe this place isn't already on Trip Advisor as we read many articles and blogs about it. I guess I'm the jerk letting the secret out. \n\nIt's a very basic banh mi. I'd say its only about 70% full and 30% just baguette, but I didn't mind as the flavors were on point. Probably best for a light lunch or afternoon snack. But If 1 doesn't fill you up then order a second for about $1 each and it'll be ready in under a minute. Starts with really great baguette, then some soft cheese, 2 types of pate, and cucumbers. At first glance I was sad about the absence of carrot/daikon/cilantro but trust me, this is a really really great banh mi. And honestly one of the top 5 best hot sauces I've ever had (and I'm a mexican food + hot sauce snob from San Diego, CA who has traveled central america and south east asia)\n\nIt's a very simple place. The friendly woman making them is situated, in typical banh mi fashion, on the sidewalk with a few tables in door behind her. She doesn't speak a lot of english, but thats fine, cause there's really only one right way to order her banh mi. Simply tell her how many you want and they will literally be done in less then 1 minute each. \n\nWhen we went her refrigerator was not working so if you really need a cold drink then maybe get the sandwiches to go. There are plenty of mini marts on the block with cold drinks. \n\nThe cherry on top of this excellent banh mi is how proud the lady is when you take pictures and she says, \"Number 1... Banh Mi!\" holding up her index finger.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 1, 2015",
